Z||000005||Dan86gt3.8||03-27-2000||12:57 PM||||There is another guy named Ted Talbert, (umm I think) in waco, I tried half harted to meet up with him once, but to no avail.  He is a member of north texas fieros.  I figure with all the people in dallas there has to be some hopped up v8 fieros running around.  I know there is a guy in houston with a pretty sweet 3.8 s/c'ed with a flame job and other goodies, plus he did the swap himself and did all the work himself.  Would love to see it but I don't frequent houston much.   ||||reg||1
Z||000006||87PegasusGT||03-27-2000||02:16 PM||||If you want to go that route, I would suggest buying from Gary's Custom Exotics. 195hp instead of 190 and also cheaper.<BR>I almost did that but after talking to Turbonetics, decided their 9.5-10:1 compression was too high to add additional boost via NOS or Turbo. 3.4 is relatively inexpensive and has a lot more hp potential plus is bone stock. You also won't have to worry about any modification to speak of (other than starter holes).||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||03-27-2000||02:53 PM||||I talked to Ed Parks at Daytona show and he is now offering 3.4s already prep to go in. According to what he said they should be around $2225 + shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mwbackus||03-27-2000||04:12 PM||||Alex:<BR>Did he say what motor that would be from?  <BR>I am thinking if it was a 3.4HT Crate it would be a damn good deal!<P>Mike ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||03-27-2000||04:25 PM||||I talked to him about the GM crate one which is what I was considering. He said that on that one once he drill the starter holes the warranty will be gone. He has a remanufactured engine supplier (Grooms Engines, of Nashville) which will sell him a 3.4 (like the crate one) and still provide 18 mo. warranty with the mods done by Ed. I think is a good deal and you save the shipping from the GM dealer to him. That's the route I will take now. ||||reg||1
